      "artist": "Anne Burgess",
      "description": "West Wing, Delgatie Castle To the west of the original castle is a curious series of additions. The nearest arch is the exterior of the chapel, then there is a room beyond. After that there is an over-ornate Gothic-style wall, which looks like the front of a doocot, but with the holes blocked with half-bricks. The final appendage resembles a mediaeval knight's tomb, but again there is just a free-standing wall with nothing behind it. In my opinion these follies detract from the simple lines of the old castle.",
